## Before Writing Any Code

{% include 'base/partials/read-patterns.md.j2' %}

**Then:**

1. `CLAUDE.md` - Project structure, technology stack, and conventions
2. Scan existing code in `src/app/`, `src/components/`, {% if variables.state_library == 'Redux Toolkit' %}`src/store/`, {% elif variables.state_library == 'Jotai' %}`src/atoms/`, {% elif variables.state_library != 'None' %}`src/stores/`, {% endif %}and `src/queries/` for established patterns

## Project Layout

All app code lives under `src/` (expo-router supports `src/app` as the routes root).
The `@/` import alias maps to `src/` (`tsconfig.json`: `"paths": { "@/*": ["./src/*"] }`).

```
src/
  app/           # expo-router routes ONLY (_layout.tsx, (tabs)/, (modals)/, [id].tsx)
  components/    # ui/, lists/, forms/
  hooks/
{% if variables.state_library == 'Redux Toolkit' %}
  store/         # Redux store, typed hooks, slices/ (UI state only, never server/DB data)
{% elif variables.state_library == 'Jotai' %}
  atoms/         # Jotai atoms (UI state only, never server/DB data)
{% elif variables.state_library != 'None' %}
  stores/        # {{ variables.state_library }} UI-state stores only (never server/DB data)
{% endif %}
  queries/       # React Query hooks + queryKeys.ts
  db/            # schema.ts, client.ts, queries/<entity>.ts, migrations/ (generated)
  i18n/          # index.ts + locales/<code>.json
{% if variables.ui_library == 'StyleSheet' %}
  constants/     # colors, spacing, typography, shadows
{% endif %}
babel.config.js  # inline-import for Drizzle .sql migrations
metro.config.js  # resolver.sourceExts += 'sql'
```

Never put non-route files (tests, helpers, components) inside `src/app/` — every file
there becomes a route.

## State Management Rules (CRITICAL)

{% if variables.state_library != 'None' %}
### {{ variables.state_library }} -- UI State ONLY

{{ variables.state_library }} holds **transient UI state** that does not originate from the server
or database. Write it as `.claude/patterns/{{ variables.state_library | lower | replace(' toolkit', '') }}.md` shows (`/new-store` generates it).

**Acceptable {{ variables.state_library }} state:**
- Loading indicators, modal visibility, bottom sheet state
- Form draft values (before submission)
- Selected tab index, filter selections, sort order
- Onboarding step, theme preference, locale selection

**NEVER put in {{ variables.state_library }}:**
- Server data (API responses)
- Database records
- Cached query results
- User profile data from the backend
{% else %}
### UI State -- Component State Only

There is no global state library. Keep transient UI state (modal visibility, drafts,
filters) in the component (`useState` / `useReducer`), lift it to the nearest common
parent, or share it via a small React context. Never copy server or database data
into component state — read it from React Query.
{% endif %}

### React Query -- Server / Database State

All data from APIs or the local database is managed via React Query.

### Drizzle ORM -- Database Operations

All database operations live in `src/db/queries/`. These are plain async functions
called from React Query hooks.

## Screen Patterns

### List Screen

{% if variables.ui_library == 'NativeWind' %}
{% raw %}
```typescript
// src/app/(tabs)/items.tsx
import { View, Text, Platform } from 'react-native';
import { Stack, Link, router } from 'expo-router';
import { FlashList } from '@shopify/flash-list';
import { useTranslation } from 'react-i18next';
import { useItems } from '@/queries/useItems';
import { ItemCard } from '@/components/lists/ItemCard';
import { EmptyState } from '@/components/ui/EmptyState';
import { FloatingActionButton } from '@/components/ui/FloatingActionButton';

export default function ItemsScreen() {
  const { t } = useTranslation();
  const { data: items, isLoading, refetch } = useItems();

  return (
    <View className="flex-1 bg-background">
      <Stack.Screen
        options={{
          title: t('items.title'),
          ...(Platform.OS === 'ios' && {
            headerRight: () => (
              <Link href="/items/new">
                <Text className="text-base font-semibold text-primary">{t('common.add')}</Text>
              </Link>
            ),
          }),
        }}
      />
      <FlashList
        data={items ?? []}
        renderItem={({ item }) => <ItemCard item={item} />}
        onRefresh={refetch}
        refreshing={isLoading}
        ListEmptyComponent={
          !isLoading ? <EmptyState message={t('items.empty')} /> : null
        }
      />
      {Platform.OS === 'android' && (
        <FloatingActionButton
          icon="plus"
          onPress={() => router.push('/items/new')}
        />
      )}
    </View>
  );
}
```
{% endraw %}
